## 5. Expected Outcome

After the checklist is prepared and applied to the dataset, the team should have:

- A list of potential data-quality issues.
- A record of checks completed and checks still pending.
- Clear rules for reviewing suspicious records.
- A better understanding of whether the dataset is ready for further processing.

## 6. Important Note

This document defines the initial data-quality checks. A check must not be marked as completed until it has actually been performed and its result recorded. The dataset must be reviewed before declaring it clean.

